sequenceDiagram
    participant C as client
    participant UI as compositor UI (wire, scene, feedback table)
    participant RT as render thread
    participant DRM as lx.drm / KMS
    participant Pres as presentation_tracker

    C->>UI: wp_presentation.feedback(surface) + wl_surface.commit
    UI->>UI: apply: feedback queued (building_frame M); the previous update's<br/>queued feedback discarded, sampled one superseded at M
    UI->>UI: tick_ui publishes frame N: visibility pass (mark_occlusion),<br/>queued feedback of on-screen surfaces sampled at N
    RT->>RT: acquire snapshot N, composite (occluded draws skipped)
    RT->>DRM: atomic commit, user_tag = N (stored before the ioctl)
    DRM-->>Pres: page_flip_event (UI): tag N, content, kernel sequence,<br/>CLOCK_MONOTONIC time, hw, vblank_timestamp
    Pres->>UI: presentation_feedback → flip handler (frame clock phase-lock)
    UI->>UI: presentation_flipped(N): sampled ≤ N presented,<br/>superseded at ≤ N discarded
    UI-->>C: sync_output(wl_output) + presented(t, refresh, seq, flags) | discarded

    Note over UI,DRM: VT switched away: everything in flight discarded at the pause edge,<br/>queued feedback discarded at each 1 Hz paused tick, nothing sampled
    Note over UI: no display (headless): a published frame counts as presented at the tick, flags 0
